# Operations Readiness Spec

## Scope

Service health, public status, incident lifecycle, backup integrity, release
verification, bounded load samples, and restore-drill evidence.

## Load when

Changing health/readiness routes, status UI, incidents, operational telemetry,
archives, migrations, deployment gates, or load/restore verification.

## Owns

- Backend domain: `backend/internal/status/`
- Routes: `/health`, `/ready`, `/api/health`, `/api/ready`, `/api/status/*`
- Incident tables: `service_incidents`, `service_incident_events`
- Migration: `backend/internal/migrations/040_service_status.sql`
- CLI operations: `internal/app/verification.go`, `internal/app/transfer.go`
- UI: `frontend/src/pages/status/StatusPage.tsx`

## Health Matrix

| Surface | Audience | Dependencies | Budget | Disclosure |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `/health` | container/node | none | local/constant | `ok` only |
| `/ready` and `/api/ready` | orchestrator | database, schema, Redis, SPA entry | 500 ms per check, parallel | generic component/state only |
| `/api/status/diagnostics` | `admin.general` | readiness set | same bounded fan-out | latency and bounded reason codes |
| `/api/status/` | public when `status` feature is explicit | readiness + published incidents | no-store | aggregate state, generic components, public incident copy |

Database, schema, Redis, and the SPA entry are required dependencies. Public
payloads never include hosts, database names, paths, exception strings, pool
credentials, stack traces, or raw telemetry. Dependency failures use the closed
reason vocabulary `dependency_unavailable` and `dependency_timeout` only.

## Incident Contracts

- Public states are investigating, monitoring, resolved, and maintenance;
  drafts are operator-only and never enter public lists.
- Components are the tenant-safe names `platform`, `web`, `database`, and
  `cache`; severity is minor, major, critical, or maintenance.
- Create/update authorization is service-enforced by `security.StatusPolicy`
  using a live `admin.general` lookup. Missing policy and lookup failure deny.
- Every write and its immutable before/after audit record commit in one
  transaction. Runtime hard delete of incident audit events is forbidden.
- Public status is opt-in through the `status` entry in `FEATURES_ENABLED`.
- Active minor/major/maintenance incidents degrade the public aggregate; active
  critical incidents make it unavailable even when dependency probes still pass.
- When enabled, `/status` is a canonical indexable SPA shell and sitemap entry;
  disabled tenants return the normal unknown-route 404/noindex response.

## Backup and Restore Contracts

| Class | Default retention | Contents/use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `migration-safety` | 7 days / newest five per tenant | SQL dump before migration/rebuild |
| `tenant-portable` | 30 days | tenant env, compose, uploads, SQL dump |
| `node-portable` | 30 days | all tenant portable data |

- Every new archive/dump is mode 0600. Its adjacent mode-0600
  `.manifest.json` sidecar contains SHA-256, byte size, class, creation time,
  retention deadline, and an explicit
  encrypted-at-rest requirement. A sidecar does not encrypt an archive; backup
  storage must provide encryption and access control before off-node retention.
- `grengo verify backup <file>` recomputes digest/size, validates archive
  metadata and required entries, and returns a machine-readable stop/proceed
  decision without extracting content.
- Restore drills use an isolated disposable database/tenant, never overwrite an
  existing tenant, verify schema plus representative row counts and `/ready`,
  record the archive digest/revision/timestamps, then remove only the named
  disposable target after evidence is retained.

## Release and Load Gates

- `grengo verify release <tenant> [--url <origin>]` records revision, a hash of
  config key names (never values), latest migration filename, bounded probe
  latency, and one `proceed`/`stop` decision.
- Required configuration, Turnstile pair consistency, liveness, readiness,
  session/Turnstile config, store reads, sitemap, and SPA checks fail closed.
- `/api/session/turnstile-config` is the public, content-free smoke probe; the
  auth-owned `user_sessions` domain remains the login/session authority.
- `grengo load-check <url>` performs read-only HTTP work with defaults of 50
  requests and four workers, hard caps of 200 and 16, a three-second request
  timeout, a 500 ms default average-latency budget, and a zero-error stop budget.
  `--websocket` caps reconnect samples to 20 attempts and four workers.
  Non-loopback targets require the
  explicit `--allow-remote` acknowledgement and must never be production or a
  third-party service.
- Load evidence records request/concurrency bounds, failures, average latency,
  and duration. Environment-specific latency, DB-pool, queue-lag, and WebSocket
  reconnect budgets must be recorded alongside the run before release.

## Verify

- `env GOCACHE=/tmp/skaia-go-cache GOTMPDIR=/tmp JWT_SECRET=test-secret go test ./...` from `backend/`
- `env GOCACHE=/tmp/skaia-go-cache GOTMPDIR=/tmp go test ./internal/app ./internal/cli`
- Frontend tests, lint, TypeScript/build, and policy checks from `frontend/`
- PostgreSQL migration rerun plus an isolated dump/restore/count/readiness drill

